        // sc-12425: the INT8-ConvRot tier's RESIDENT VRAM ceiling, now MEASURED (sc-12381) — 42.9 GB
        // overall-peak on an exclusive sm_120 at 1024²/8-step, the same shape used for the standard tiers.
        // This is the TE-CO-RESIDENT peak; the tier's efficient footprint is `sequentialPeakGb` (28.6).
        //
        // It replaces sc-9300's estimate of 31.0, which was wrong by 11.9 GB. That estimate blamed "the
        // online Hadamard rotation adds transient activation"; the real cause is duller — ConvRot loads
        // the Qwen3-VL text encoder at f32 (15.6 GB) and, pinned Resident, held it through the whole
        // denoise. So 42.9 lands ABOVE q8's 35.9 purely on the f32 TE, NOT on anything int8-specific: the
        // int8 DiT is the same size as q8's, and once the TE drops the two tiers match (28.6 vs 29.5
        // sequential). (42.9 is itself post-sc-12301, which removed 7.4 GB of duplicated per-projection
        // cuBLASLt workspace; pre-fix this tier peaked at 50.3 GB.)
        //
        // The 31.0 survived because NOTHING READ IT: `vram_gate::requested_tier_key` is bits-derived and
        // a ConvRot request carries no `mlxQuantize`, so it fell to `"q8"` and this row was dead. Fixed in
        // `base.rs` (`INT8_CONVROT_TIER`) — so this number is now load-bearing. It is the RESIDENT need
        // that decides fit-then-fall-back: a card too small for 42.9 drops to the sequential path (28.6)
        // rather than being rejected — which the pinned inference rev (d64af1dd, contains PR #67) now
        // honors, so the ConvRot lane actually drops its TE under `OffloadPolicy::Sequential`. Re-measure
        // both with `krea_probed_generate_for_offload_ab` (`KREA_CONVROT_DIT`, resident vs
        // spec-sequential), NOT by re-estimating.
        //
        // Gates the `int8-convrot` variant through the SAME per-tier memory-eligibility path as
        // q4/q8/bf16 (the third of the three ConvRot gates; the candle lane + sm_89 compute-cap are the
        // worker's `int8_convrot` capability).
        // sc-12828 RE-MEASURED int8-convrot: 42.9 → 34.7 GB. The pinned inference (fc1654a9, PR #101)
        // now stores the Qwen3-VL TE bf16 (f32 compute, bit-identical) instead of at f32, so the f32-TE
        // co-resident buffer this ConvRot RESIDENT peak was inflated by is halved. Measured on that
        // pinned build, exclusive sm_120, 1024²/8-step seed 42: steady 29.76 → 21.5 GB, overall-peak
        // 42.9 → 34.7 GB — a constant 8.2 GB shift = the 15.6 → 7.4 GB dense TE reduction, landing
        // int8-convrot right next to q8 as the sc-12425 note predicted ("once the TE drops the two tiers
        // match").
        // sc-13108 directly re-measured the standard tiers on the pinned bf16-TE build, exclusive
        // RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell sm_120, 1024²/8-step seed 42. Resident/sequential raw pixels were
        // byte-identical per tier. q4/q8 fall only 0.7 GB because their TEs are packed; the dense bf16
        // tier realizes the full win (55.6 → 47.2 GB). These are measured peaks, not derived shifts.
        "vramGbByTier": { "q4": 25.7, "q8": 35.2, "bf16": 47.2, "int8-convrot": 34.7 },
        "vramMeasuredPixels": 1048576,
        // sc-12131 / sc-10856 second-stage gate: measured largest working set after the text phase has
        // been dropped. sc-13108 directly measured q4/q8/bf16 at 21.9/29.4/39.4 GB; sc-12425 measured
        // int8-convrot at 28.6 GB with resident/sequential byte-identical pixels. The int8 and q8 DiTs
        // remain close in size once their text encoders are dropped, so their sequential peaks converge.
        "sequentialPeakGb": { "q4": 21.9, "q8": 29.4, "bf16": 39.4, "int8-convrot": 28.6 },
        // sc-15117: quality-preserving Q4 constrained-card fit ladder. Each phase is
        // `fixedGb + perMpxGb * megapixels`; the worker adds its normal 2 GiB safety reserve and selects
        // the first sufficient rung in declaration order. Curves are conservative upper fits (+~0.1 GiB
        // calibration allowance) to rendered-device samples at 768² and 1024², seed 42, on an exclusive
        // RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell with the public q4 turnkey. Step count does not change the working set.
        //
        // ==> SUPERSEDED BY sc-17097. The sc-15117/15205/15206/16514 sample tables below describe the
        // calibration-ABI-1 captures and are retained as provenance for how this block was originally
        // derived. They are NOT the shipped curves: `turboFit.phaseCurvesByTier` is now fitted from the
        // ABI-3 re-measurement, whose raw samples are tabulated in Shortcut sc-17097 activity 17466 and
        // reproduced per cell in each `evidenceRecords` entry's `observedPhasesGb` / `observedPeaksGb`.
        // The methodology is unchanged (exclusive rendered-device phase peaks at 768² and 1024²); the
        // instrument is now the versioned harness (`sceneworks-memory-v5`, 30 cells, --fresh-per-case)
        // rather than an ad-hoc capture, and every fitted curve is pinned at or above BOTH measured
        // geometries so no measured point can be under-predicted.
        //
        // Superseded ABI-1 raw sample peaks (GiB):
        //   threeStage       768² text/denoise/decode 3.895/11.747/10.843;
        //                    1024²                         3.895/15.405/15.440
        //   tiledVae        768²                           3.895/11.747/9.702;
        //                    1024²                         3.895/15.405/9.736
        //   chunkedAttention 768²                          3.895/11.076/9.702;
        //                    1024²                         3.895/11.345/9.702
        //   streamedBlocks  768²                           3.895/3.761/4.736;
        //                    1024²                         3.895/4.063/5.676
        // sc-15205 adds the equivalent Q8 matrix from the same exclusive hardware/methodology; no Q4
        // curve was scaled or reused. Raw Q8 phase samples (GiB):
        //   threeStage       768² text/denoise/decode 6.345/18.357/16.514;
        //                    1024²                         6.345/22.015/16.514
        //   tiledVae         768²                          6.345/18.357/16.548;
        //                    1024²                         6.345/22.015/16.514
        //   chunkedAttention 768²                          6.345/17.619/16.514;
        //                    1024²                         6.345/18.156/16.512
        //   streamedBlocks   768²                          6.345/6.211/4.837;
        //                    1024²                         6.847/6.757/4.132
        // sc-15206 adds the dense BF16 matrix, again from direct production-weight measurements rather
        // than scaling either packed tier. Raw BF16 phase samples (GiB):
        //   threeStage       768² text/denoise/decode 8.694/28.390/26.413;
        //                    1024²                         8.694/32.014/26.446
        //   tiledVae         768²                          8.694/28.390/26.446;
        //                    1024²                         8.560/32.014/26.446
        //   chunkedAttention 768²                          8.527/27.552/26.414;
        //                    1024²                         8.526/27.652/26.413
        //   streamedBlocks   768²                          8.535/8.533/2.130;
        //                    1024²                         8.526/8.526/3.629
        // sc-16514 recovered the already-captured 768² cells into machine-readable evidence from
        // sc-15205 activity 15272 (Q8) and sc-15206 activity 15314 (BF16), then independently fitted
        // every tier from its own 768²→1024² delta. Q8's three-stage/tiled-VAE denoise slope happens
        // to equal Q4's 7.98 GiB/MP because both measured deltas are 3.658 GiB; it is not borrowed.
        // Retained zero slopes are measured flat/decreasing phases: Q8 three-stage decode 16.514→
        // 16.514, tiled decode 16.548→16.514, chunked decode 16.514→16.512, and streamed decode
        // 4.837→4.132; BF16 tiled decode 26.446→26.446, chunked decode 26.414→26.413, and streamed
        // text/denoise 8.535→8.526 / 8.533→8.526. BF16 three-stage decode 26.413→26.446 is positive,
        // so its former zero slope is replaced by the independently fitted 0.08 GiB/MP curve below.
        // Tiled decode is a measured no-op for the denoise-owned Q8/BF16 peaks, so those curves
        // intentionally cannot displace the cheaper three-stage rung.
        "turboFit": {
          // sc-15449 shared memory-strategy selector provenance. The worker accepts these measured curves
          // only while both source revisions and the provider request ABI fingerprint match.
          //
          // sc-16211 replaces sc-15994's catalog-wide fingerprint tombstone with an exact
          // measured-composition identity per rung. SC-16402 corrects the provider contract to attest
          // the physical staged-residency path already present in the tiled-VAE, chunked-attention,
          // and streamed-block captures, so every measured row binds to its exact executed composition.
          //
          // sc-17097 re-collects every cell below under `gen_core::MEMORY_CALIBRATION_ABI` 3. The ABI
          // moved 1 -> 2 (typed load shape, inference sc-16583) -> 3 (typed reference-count geometry,
          // inference 5083b0ec), and each bump declares earlier records intentionally stale. Stamping 3
          // onto the ABI-1 curves would have silenced the handshake while leaving a fit measured under
          // different semantics, which is exactly what the handshake exists to stop - and the numbers
          // moved, so it would also have shipped wrong ones. Every tier's three-stage peak is now
          // materially HIGHER than the ABI-1 curve it replaces (q4 1024^2 15.44 -> 21.285 GiB, q8
          // 22.015 -> 25.911, bf16 32.014 -> 36.724): the superseded manifest UNDER-predicted the rung
          // a constrained card falls to first, while the deeper bounded rungs got cheaper.
          //
          // `loadShape` is the ABI-2 axis made load-bearing on this route. The worker used to take the
          // shape from the provider alone, so the axis did no work here; it now compares this declared
          // shape against the provider identity and refuses a fit measured under the other one.
          "calibrationAbi": 3,
          "loadShape": "deferred_materialization",
          "calibrationFingerprint": "krea-turbo-cuda-phase-curves-v1",
          "sceneWorksRevision": "sc-15449-contract-v1",
          // Inference revision these curves are declared COMPATIBLE with. The campaign measured against
          // 277f4238 (kept verbatim in every record's own `inferenceCommit` receipt, which is never
          // rewritten); this declaration moved to the sc-15819 closeout pin only after verifying that the
          // one-commit range has an EMPTY diff against both `candle-gen-krea` and
          // `gen-core/src/memory_strategy.rs`. The fingerprint is unchanged because the provider's tensor
          // layout, quantization floors and execution structure did not move - only the shared contract
          // ABI did, which is precisely the split the two identity fields exist to express.
          "inferenceRevision": "a4f409ae8ce73eda2ee8117b89b5f479666606b8",
          // sc-17774: the currency term. `inferenceRevision` above is capture provenance and is
          // no longer compared — the digest of `candle-gen-krea`'s compile closure is.
          "inferenceClosureDigest": "bdf379ae9f95302f2010f859eae6806b6382c22d9dffd36c51059d440548f03f",
          // sc-17989: names the closure lane (`candle:` + this) so `backfill-closure-digests.mjs`
          // can pair the two keys above and re-derive the digest under `--verify`, like every
          // per-binding calibration. Before this key the digest was maintained by hand, ungraded.
          "provider": "krea_2_turbo",
          "measured": true,
          "verification": {
            "hardware": "RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (sm_120)",
            "stories": ["sc-15117", "sc-15205", "sc-15206", "sc-17097"],
            "method": "exclusive rendered-device phase peaks at 768x768 and 1024x1024",
            "numericPolicy": "selector boundary exact; phase-curve golden tolerance 0.01 GiB; every fitted curve pinned at or above BOTH measured geometries after rounding, so no measured point can be under-predicted",
            "outputParity": "ordinary CUDA text-to-image retains tier and output bytes; sc-17097 additionally compares a resident render against the deepest bounded rung from one loaded generator per tier, after proving the resident A-B-A repeat is bit-identical"
          },
          // Machine-readable evidence cells. Each row's `sceneWorksCommit` / `capturedAt` name its
          // PHASE capture; the `parity` block on an `exact_request` row comes from a second run of the
          // same source tree (the five-rung lane measures per-rung memory but compares no outputs, so
          // parity needs the resident-versus-bounded lane). Both runs are recorded in sc-17097
          // activity 17466 with their own timestamps.
          //
          // `exact_request` rows carry geometry-specific output
          // parity and may admit that exact request after runtime fingerprint/loadability checks.
          // `phase_fit_only` rows carry direct per-phase measurements that determine a bounded curve,
          // but cannot authorize runtime admission without parity for that same geometry. Observed
          // values come from the cited Shortcut activities; artifact revisions name the merged path.
          "evidenceRecords": [
            {
