      "limits": {
        "durations": [3, 4, 5],
        "recommendedMaxDuration": 5,
        "hardMaxDuration": 5,
        "fps": [16],
        // A14B rides the z16 Wan2.1 VAE: `patch (1,2,2)` × `vae_stride (4,8,8)` = **16**.
        // The constraint is the engines' own divisibility check — candle
        // `SIZE_MULTIPLE_14B = 16` enforced via `is_multiple_of`
        // (candle-gen-wan/src/config.rs:209, checked at wan14b.rs:635), and mlx's
        // `align_dim(patch, vae_stride)` (mlx-gen-wan/src/pipeline.rs:36, config.rs:169).
        // (The descriptor `min_size` agrees by convention, but it is only a lower BOUND —
        // gen-core checks `req.width < min_size` — not a lattice.) Only the dense TI2V-5B
        // needs 32 (its z48 VAE has vae_stride 16). Declaring 16 is the engine's truth and
        // keeps custom dims honest (sc-12294).
        //
        // The 720p buckets are TRUE 720p. `720 = 45·16` is on the stride above, and the A14B's
        // **area** cap is upstream's own `1280*720` = 921,600 (`MAX_AREA_CONFIGS[t2v-A14B]` in
        // Wan2.2's wan/configs/__init__.py — the same set i2v-A14B and Wan2.1's vace-14B get).
        // 1280x720 sits exactly AT the cap (the check is `>`), so it renders as advertised.
        //
        // These buckets read 1280x704 until sc-12308. That is the TI2V-5B's geometry, and it was
        // adopted here only because MAX_AREA_14B had borrowed the 5B's 901,120 budget — a number
        // whose 704 comes from the 5B's 32-px grid, not from any 14B limit. Being 2.3% low, it
        // excluded exactly the canonical 720p: candle hard-errored on it, mlx i2v silently refit it
        // to 1264x704, and the manifest was walked down to match rather than the cap questioned.
        //
        // `maxPixels` makes the cap ENFORCED rather than merely advertised: nothing in the app
        // validates against `resolutions`, so a raw over-cap request (job retry, MCP, preset replay)
        // reaches the engine untouched. The backends now AGREE — candle rejects above MAX_AREA_14B
        // (candle-gen-wan/src/wan14b.rs:645) and mlx rejects too (its T2V `max_area: 0` is gone;
        // model.rs `validate_impl` → `reject_over_area`), both at 921,600.
        "requiresDimensionsMultipleOf": 16,
        "maxPixels": 921600,
        "resolutions": ["832x480", "480x832", "1280x720", "720x1280"],
        // Epic 7114 curated menu (sc-7296). Base = the candle (Windows) A14B engine's curated
        // set (native `uni_pc`/`euler`); the macOS mlx override below exposes the full curated
        // fold-in. No scheduler axis (flow shift = `scheduler_shift`).
        "samplers": ["default", "uni_pc", "euler"],
        "schedulers": ["default"]
      },
      "loraCompatibility": {
        "families": ["wan-video"],
        "types": ["style", "motion", "character", "enhance"]
      },
      // GGUF-quantized A14B experts for the torch adapter. A14B is GPU-heavy at bf16
      // (~56GB transformers), so quantization is the default on both platforms: Q8_0
      // on MPS (trivial dequant, ~3x slower vs ~13x for k-quants), Q4_K_M on CUDA
      // (smallest, fused kernel). Two experts: high-noise -> transformer, low-noise
