      // sc-17632 (epic 17625) — the OTHER upscaler, and the same story as SAM3 below: SeedVR2 had
      // no install-flow representation at all. Its repo and pinned revision lived only as
      // hardcoded constants in worker source, DUPLICATED across the two lanes that load it — the
      // `image_upscale` job (`upscale_jobs.rs`) and the `video_upscale` job
      // (`video_jobs/seedvr2.rs`) — and each lane downloaded the SAME ~7.3 GB checkpoint mid-render
      // into its OWN destination (`<data_dir>/cache/upscale/seedvr2/` and
      // `<data_dir>/cache/seedvr2-mlx/`), where the Models screen can neither size nor delete it.
      //
      // The loader half landed with this entry: both lanes now call ONE cache-only resolver,
      // `upscale_jobs::require_seedvr2_checkpoint_dir`. Declaring the repo WITHOUT that change
      // would have been worse than leaving it alone — install state keys on the declared repo, so
      // the entry would have flipped every existing install to "not installed", prompted a 7.3 GB
      // download the loaders ignored, and then still fetched the same bytes inside the next render.
      //
      // Migration: an existing install keeps working from EITHER legacy root, so nothing
      // re-downloads. Those bytes are now orphaned — never written to again, and not reachable from
      // this entry's artifact paths. Reclaiming them is tracked on sc-17636 (S11), which owns
      // delete/size coverage.
      //
      // The revision is byte-for-byte the worker's own `SEEDVR2_REVISION` (`upscale_jobs.rs`,
      // sc-8879), and the files are the upstream names verbatim — the engine loads them unrenamed,
      // straight out of the HF snapshot dir. They MUST agree: `SEEDVR2_REVISION` is a 40-hex pin,
      // so the resolver reads that EXACT `snapshots/<sha>/` with no fall-through to `refs/main`,
      // and a manifest installing a different one would report "installed" while every SeedVR2 job
      // failed with "not installed". `manifest_declares_the_same_seedvr2_pin_the_loader_reads`
      // (upscale_jobs/tests.rs) fails if either side drifts.
